{"availability":"available","full":"Bitcoin-PIR/Bitcoin-PIR","name":"Bitcoin-PIR","description":"Implementing PIR for Bitcoin UTXO set","category":"Finance","language":"Rust","stars":16,"forks":1,"created":"2026-03-13T02:43:36Z","updated":"2026-10-11T03:37:15Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://www.bitcoinpir.org/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:32.458Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:32.458Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:32.458Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:32.458Z","stars":16,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Query the Bitcoin UTXO set without revealing which addresses you're interested in.","Today's light wallets leak every address you own to their server, enabling full surveillance of your balances, transactions, and spending habits. Bitcoin PIR uses Private Information Retrieval — a family of cryptographic protocols where the server(s) provably learn nothing about which records you look up — to give light wallets the same privacy as a full node, without the storage cost."],"features":["Each UTXO lookup can be paired with a Merkle proof query that checks the result against the database's Merkle root. Verification is batched across all addresses in a wallet sync — one proof round covers the whole batch.…","Trust-model note on Merkle verification. Clients check each result's Merkle proof and report the verdict per result (merkleVerified); the caller decides what to do with an unverified one. A client can also verify the…","Wallet sync typically touches dozens of addresses at once. Bitcoin PIR packs multiple addresses into a single PIR round using probabilistic batch codes, so syncing a wallet with 50 addresses takes roughly the same time…","The server hosts the complete Bitcoin UTXO set (815K active script types at time of writing), filtered to exclude dust and very heavy addresses. Light wallets see the same data a full node would return.","Anyone can run PIR servers from a public Bitcoin Core snapshot. Free queries are open; a provider chooses per backend what is free, paid, or free while the server has room, and paid queries present credits verified at…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Bitcoin-PIR/Bitcoin-PIR/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"85188938ae43b5fe8cdf9c502a87112e03376e8561af070937ff34900b4508a0","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:32.537Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:32.537Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Query the Bitcoin UTXO set without revealing which addresses you're interested in.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Bitcoin-PIR/Bitcoin-PIR/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"85188938ae43b5fe8cdf9c502a87112e03376e8561af070937ff34900b4508a0","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Bitcoin-PIR/Bitcoin-PIR/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:32.538Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-11T03:37:15Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Bitcoin-PIR/Bitcoin-PIR/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:32.539Z","hash":"85188938ae43b5fe8cdf9c502a87112e03376e8561af070937ff34900b4508a0","originalBytes":9818,"storedBytes":9818,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["server","docs","bitcoin","database","pir","merkle","production","query","see","each","proof","root","verification","addresses","one","onionpir","oram","privacy","queries","any","build","direct","harmonypir","utxo","wallet","which","backends","client","full","result","round","sync","wallets","without","batch","browser","chunk","count","host","index","license","need","note","operations.md","overview.md","same","servers","single","testing.md","web","address","attestation","attested","backend","before","bitcoin-pir","channel","clients","core","cryptographic","data","demo","documentation","does","dpf","dpf-pir","every","found","free","light","live","lookups","open","operator","own","runs","r